{"schema":"semaprax.bend2-law-benchmark.boolean-edit-response.v1","trial_id":"scalar-contract-bug-v1:semaprax-scalar-v1:10","language":"semaprax-scalar-v1","final_source":"module app;

// Mutant control: the checked postcondition retains total Boolean negation,
// but the implementation always returns false. The runtime route must refuse.
@id("app.negate")
fn negate(value: bool) -> bool
    ensures result == !value
{
    !value
}

@id("app.main")
fn main() -> i64
{
    if negate(false) { 0 } else { 1 }
}
","proof_explanation":"The implementation returns the Boolean negation of its input, satisfying the stated postcondition for both Boolean inputs. Thus negate(false) is true, so the success witness is accepted. The seeded mutant returning false violates the postcondition at input false and is rejected. This is an agent claim, not proof execution.","seeded_attack":{"source_sha256":"sha256:9f6aab36ed9d03ede8e3cb1f79407e77f8fe5395434a6b8579acc59e7270ba2b","decision":"reject","reason":"Its constant-false implementation violates the retained ensures result == !value contract when value is false."}}
